[31m-## 8. Methodology summary[m
[31m-* **Preprocessing:** timestamp parsing and validation; duplicate policy (none found); missing data are explicit `?`/empty rows. Hourly **mean over observed minutes**; an hour is valid only with ≥ 45/60 observed minutes; sub-meter energy = mean × 60 (Wh/h); causal forward-fill (≤ 3 h) for *inputs only*, flagged; evaluated targets never imputed; longer gaps stay missing. A masking experiment compares fill strategies. Outliers kept (plausible peaks).[m
[31m-* **Analytical questions (Section 11):** Q1 trend; Q2 hour-of-day / weekday patterns; Q3 relationships with other measurements; **Q4 lagged features (ACF/PACF)**; **Q5 moving averages (smoothing, delay, leakage-safe shifted MAs)**; Q6 predictive usefulness of lag/MA/historical-mean predictors. Q4–Q6 use only the first 80 % of the timeline so the test period is never examined.[m
[31m-* **Features (31):** lags 1,2,3,6,12,24,48,168 of the target; rolling mean/SD over 3,6,24,168 h computed on the *shifted* series; lag-1 of the other measurements; calendar features of the *predicted* hour. Verified by assertions and a "corrupt-the-future" leakage test.[m
[31m-* **Split:** chronological 70/15/15 (train/validation/test); `TimeSeriesSplit` (4 folds) for tuning inside the training set only.[m
[31m-* **Models:** persistence and seasonal-naive baselines; Ridge; Random Forest; tuned versions (grid search for Ridge, randomised search for RF); ablation with target-only features. **Selection uses validation MAE only**; test metrics are reported afterwards.[m
[31m-* **Metrics:** MAE (primary), RMSE, R²; MAPE (test, supplementary; only valid because actual values are > 0.05 kW).[m
